            </div>
          </div>
          <div wb-interval-delay="0.2" wb-component="smart-animate" class="_2-columns">
            <div id="w-node-cf4dfba4-6c3d-8882-fd66-a19d22296fae-d28188ac" class="card-contaiiner fill-height">
              <div class="card cursor obrizum">
                <div class="video yt-our-work"><video muted="" loop="" webkit-playsinline="" playsinline="" autoplay="true" class="video-card-visual__video h-auto">
                    <source src="https://motiontheagency.b-cdn.net/Case%20studies/Obrizum/obrizum%20clip-1%20(2).mp4" type="video/mp4">
                  </video></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="w-layout-vflex list-wrap no-top-margin">
              <div class="text-14-150-3 opacity-80">Obrizum needed support on both their <a href="https://www.motiontheagency.com/blog/b2b-vs-b2c-explainer-videos-whats-the-difference-why-it-matters" class="link-33">clients&#x27; projects and their internal needs,</a> covering Learning and Development content as well as marketing purposes. They required a steady flow of video content, from product<a href="/services/explainer-video" class="link-30"> explainers </a>to brand and marketing animations, but with traditional pricing, scaling that output would’ve been costly. With our <a href="/pricing/design-subscription-services" class="link-31">subscription model,</a> everything became simpler — one flat monthly rate, unlimited projects, and a dedicated team ready to jump in whenever needed.</div>
